# CR 702.35: Fiery Temper discarded to pay Tormenting Voice's additional cost
# is discarded into exile (Madness's Discard$ replacement,
# CardFactoryUtil.java:2345-2362), and its "when you do, cast it for its
# madness cost" trigger (:1386-1420) waits until Tormenting Voice is on the
# stack, then goes above it (PlaySpellAbility.java:682 freezes the stack while
# the cost is paid; TriggerHandler.java:264). So Fiery Temper is cast for {R}
# and resolves first: the graveyard holds it under Tormenting Voice.
startturn human
advance 3
tapformana human 3 R
tapformana human 4 R
tapformana human 5 R
# Tormenting Voice: {1}{R}, discard Fiery Temper.
queue paygeneric R
queue discardchoice 2
# The madness trigger: cast Fiery Temper (the single Optional$ choice),
# targeting the opponent.
queue confirmeffect true
queue targets ai
castspell human 1
resolvestack
